    "The boundary-enforcement harness (trybuild compile-fail cases, the syn-based no-raw-primitive scanner) — deferred by SPEC-ARCH-003 to its own future sibling spec, which was never split out as of this writing. This spec does not gate on that harness existing; it relies on the same two enforcement mechanisms SPEC-ARCH-003 shipped without the harness: the module-level clippy `#[deny(...)]` (already in place) and a plain-substring residual-coercion test (extended by this spec, see scope).",
