d the just-added, not-yet-committed test); resolved by staging the file with `git add` before sabotaging, so `git checkout --` restores to the staged (test-present, sabotage-absent) version instead of HEAD. (3) T8's residual-coercion-scan update gets a genuine, non-sabotaged red phase for free: the existing test's hard-coded `== 1` cast-allow-count assertion is already false the moment T6 lands (is_retryable_status's allow is deleted), so running the untouched test against the already-migrated tree fails naturally — no fabrication needed there. Numeric expected values for AC-025 through AC-029 (110, 220, 100, 500, null) were derived directly from crates/michi-resilience/src/lib.rs's next_retry_delay arithmetic (`raw_ms = base_ms * 2^attempt`, `jitter_ms = (raw_ms as f64 * jitter_factor * jitter_seed) as u64`, `capped_ms = jittered_ms.max(retry_after_ms).min(max_ms)`), read fresh rather than assumed, so every Node-level acceptance test asserts an exact number instead of a vague 'succeeds'.",
